  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe model importer expands `GUAC` and `SUNT` in the parsed STEP records.\nThe unit checks and topology reader then use the same long names.\nShort-name inch and metre models keep their correct size in millimetres.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe pinned parser expands some short names but leaves these two unchanged.\nThe unit reader only finds the long names.\nIt can miss the unit context and silently assume millimetres.\n\nThe mappings come from the public [ISO short-name registry](https://standards.iso.org/iso/10303/tech/short_names/short-names.txt).\nThe fixtures use our unit-box geometry.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `short_name_inch_import_keeps_scale`\n- `short_name_metre_import_keeps_scale`\n- `short_context_only_import_keeps_scale`\n- `short_si_unit_only_import_keeps_scale`\n- `long_name_context_controls_import_with_correct_scale`\n\nThe four regression tests failed before the fix. The long-name controls passed.\nAll five tests pass with the fix.\nThe tests check the units, solid count, bounding coordinates, and volume.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Restoring the full upstream source makes all four regressions fail. Restoring the fix passes all five tests.\n- Removing the `GUAC` mapping fails its isolated test. Restoring it passes.\n- Removing the `SUNT` mapping fails its isolated test. Restoring it passes.\n\nThe two new fixture rows are in `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement/rows.rs` after the merge of main.\n`step_short_units_inch` and `step_short_units_metre` remain.\nThe rows keep the recorded legacy reader refusals.\nThe removed reader stays removed.\n`recorded_truck_readings_keep_their_findings` checks both refusal readings.\nRemoving each row makes its per-file test fail. Restoring each row passes.\nChanging each refusal makes the preservation pin fail. Restoring each refusal passes.\n\nFinal validation on head `20214c9f8cd0f1614e415281a3b69ce389c25d7c`:\n\n- STEP agreement suite: 25 tests passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: all 82 steps passed; 2046 tests passed; 33 ignored; 13.1 minutes.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: all 249 steps passed; 44.2 minutes.\n- Kernel heavy lane: passed; 4 tests passed.\n- Motion heavy lane: passed; 56 tests passed.\n- App heavy lane: passed; 41 tests passed.\n- Known-fail checks: all nine checks failed at their expected assertions and passed the gate checks.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed; exit 0; 51.6 seconds.\n\nThe final gates ran on this unchanged head.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` files changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine, release gate, or manual GUI import was exercised.\nThis change does not repair the raw tessellator or the legacy STEP reader.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes the touched files.\nPR #2918 changes the tool-body reader in other files.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: STEP model import preserves inch and metre scale when unit entities use ISO short names.\n\nFixes #2919\n\n",
